Note that it requests geometrically more for each gift.  By the time
you have 10 artifacts the chances are 1-in-210.  But there's good
news here for the partient - Offering only 1000 monster in a massive
sacfest is likely to get you several.  Yeah, only a thousand, chuckle.

Also note that gifts and artifats aren't *quite* the same.  Every gift
is an artifact but there are several other ways to get artifacts.
Before
your first gift it doesn't matter how many artifacts you have
accumulated.  Find Cleaver in a armorry shop, name Sting, get
Frost Bane from a bones file, kill something for Sunsword and so
on and the very first gift still has a 1-in-10 chance per offering.  In
most cases the only impact this has is the two namable ones and
any bones files.

But get that first gift and every artifact seen in the game (including
any you vaporized) count against you for further gifts.  Do the Quest
and bingo your chances go down because now you have more
artifacts.



